      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please update the commit message to use concise prose instead of a bulleted walkthrough of C macros/operators, and avoid joining distinct change categories in the subject line:\n\n1. **Prose Over Code Narration:** Instead of listing low-level expressions (`newrange`, `LSM6DSM_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(newrange)`, `__fls()`, `\u003e` vs. `\u003c`, `s-\u003ecurrent_range`) in bullets, explain *why* the prior behavior failed and *what* changed conceptually in 1–2 short prose paragraphs.\n2. **Undocumented `prj.conf` Change \u0026 Scope Split:** `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dsm/prj.conf` (`CONFIG_SENSOR\u003dy`) is not mentioned in the commit message and should be either dropped (since `EMUL_LSM6DSM` already selects `SENSOR` in `zephyr/emul/Kconfig`) or moved to a separate test-config CL. Similarly, if splitting the normalization/round-up fix and the min/max clamping change into separate CLs, use focused descriptions for each.\n\n**Option A (If split into focused CLs):**\n\n- **CL 1 (Normalization and round-up fix):**\n```text\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dsm: Normalize rounded accel range in set_range\n\nPreviously, set_range() for MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL compared the\nrequested range against the rounded-down power-of-two range using `\u003c`\ninstead of `\u003e`, preventing non-power-of-two ranges from rounding up\nwhen requested, and stored the un-normalized range in current_range.\n\nNormalize the accelerometer full-scale range to a supported power of\ntwo and double it when round-up is requested on a non-power-of-two\ninput.\n\nBUG\u003db:574009676\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dsm\n\nChange-Id: I7ef3dad4fb0cb5bba0ac26d5ea3be01ec8774188\n```\n\n- **CL 2 (Clamping out-of-bounds accelerometer ranges):**\n```text\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dsm: Clamp accel range in set_range\n\nAccelerometer full-scale ranges below 2G were passed directly into\n__fls() without lower-bound clamping, resulting in invalid bit shifts\nand register encodings.\n\nDefine LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL (2G) and clamp requested accelerometer\nranges to [LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL] before\nnormalizing.\n\nBUG\u003db:574009676\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dsm\n```\n\n**Option B (If kept as a single CL after removing the unrelated `prj.conf` change):**\n```text\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dsm: Fix accel range normalization in set_range\n\nPreviously, set_range() for MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL did not clamp\ninputs below the minimum 2G full-scale range, checked `\u003c` instead of\n`\u003e` when rounding up non-power-of-two ranges, and stored the\nun-normalized range in current_range.\n\nClamp requested accelerometer ranges to [2G, 16G], normalize to a\nsupported power-of-two full-scale value, and round up to the next\npower of two when requested.\n\nBUG\u003db:574009676\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dsm\n\nChange-Id: I7ef3dad4fb0cb5bba0ac26d5ea3be01ec8774188\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/0badb717-4734-4ea1-bdc8-e5eb907799f5)",
