      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Once the requested range is clamped to `[LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL, LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL]` (`[2, 16]`), normalizing `range` up front eliminates the second `LSM6DSM_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS()` call and makes the `if (newrange \u003e LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL)` branch unreachable:\n\n- Because `LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL` (`16`) is already a power of two, `range \u003e newrange` (`16 \u003e 16`) is false at the upper bound, and for any clamped `range \u003c 16`, `LSM6DSM_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(range)` is at most `8`, so doubling it when `rnd` is set produces at most `16` and already yields a normalized power-of-two value in `{2, 4, 8, 16}`.\n\nConsider simplifying this block to match the pattern in `driver/accel_lis2dw12.c`:\n\n```c\n\tcase MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL:\n\t\trange \u003d CLAMP(range, LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MIN_VAL,\n\t\t\t      LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_MAX_VAL);\n\t\tnewrange \u003d LSM6DSM_ACCEL_NORMALIZE_FS(range);\n\n\t\t/* Adjust and check rounded value for acc. */\n\t\tif (rnd \u0026\u0026 (range \u003e newrange))\n\t\t\tnewrange *\u003d 2;\n\n\t\treg_val \u003d LSM6DSM_ACCEL_FS_REG(newrange);\n\t\tbreak;\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/0badb717-4734-4ea1-bdc8-e5eb907799f5)",
